  "title": "In Fano trees every atom is a block, and a line receives creation exactly where it touches the cut toward it",
  "subject": "What the screening lemmas prove about the brace dictionary",
  "conclusion": "In spaces built from Fano atoms alone, creation in the chain of atoms between two lines implies creation in the whole space, so every atom is a block and every line that touches its atom's cut toward a removal at most two atoms away receives creation from it. On every chain computed, that touching is also necessary: the dictionary is one rule, with non-creation still resting on the pendant-line statement.",
